### 2. Harness side — timer push wrapper (`js/timerAutoCommitAndSave.js`)

The bare `git push origin HEAD` must self-heal on non-fast-forward: catch push error → check if it's a non-FF rejection → `git fetch origin <branch>` + `git merge --no-edit origin/<branch>`... wait, the ticket says `git pull --no-rebase`. But note the timer works in the TARGET repo workingDir, branch = current HEAD. The existing pushReworkChanges already has this pattern:

```js
cmd('git -c fetch.recurseSubmodules=no fetch origin ' + branchName + ':refs/remotes/origin/' + branchName);
cmd('git merge --no-edit origin/' + branchName);
cmd('git push -u origin ' + branchName);
```

That's the "fetch + merge + push" self-heal already in pushReworkChanges! So pushReworkChanges ALREADY self-heals non-FF (fetch origin branch, merge, retry push once). The remaining bare push is the TIMER's `git push origin HEAD` in `timerAutoCommitAndSave.js` — that's the one from the incident ("⏱️ timer: git push failed").

